  "lineage": "Mid-1990s-and-2000s Memphis Tennessee hip-hop subgenre characterized by dark-ominous-horror-influenced production (drawing on horror-film soundtrack samples), ultra-slow tempo with chopped vocal-delivery, and graphic violence-and-drug lyrical content. Three 6 Mafia (Memphis 1991-onward, founded by DJ Paul and Juicy J) is the canonical type-specimen with their 1995 Mystic Stylez and 2005 Academy-Award win for Hustle & Flow. Direct ancestor of phonk subgenre.",
